k recently downgraded Finstad's prospects, citing a favorable climate for Democrats.\n\nThere are no reliable general-election polls, and the available surveys are old and sponsored by partisan groups. Jake Johnson has raised nearly as much as Finstad and has campaigned aggressively across the district's 21 counties, but he is a teacher and first-time candidate in red turf. The prediction markets put his chances near 26 percent. The forecast sits at roughly R+4.5 with wide uncertainty, a Lean R race that could tighten if the national environment keeps breaking Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1904, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2716, "margin": -4.5}]}